Cell["\<\



t(u), x(u), \:1e6b(u), \:1e8b(u) in the complex proper-time plane, plotted \
with ColorFunction \[RightArrow] \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]CyclicReImLogAbs\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] (compare Fig. 2 of the paper). Red means real and \
positive, blue real and negative; black lines are lines of constant real or \
imaginary part.

The Im = 0 curves of t, x, \:1e6b, \:1e8b are overlaid in the last plot: the \
contour turns horizontal where they intersect.


\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.0031922447881546`*^9, 
  4.0031922539163*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"94b2e84d-a87c-6649-a2ed-56b37b1e9382"],

